    <bpmn:process id="W_W3418" name="W3418. Rapid Commodity-Shock Price Response &amp; Margin Recovery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Market shock (W3407); sudden cost surge; supply disruption (links to VS-69/VS-02.3)
Frequency: Event-driven
Volume: Affected categories/SKUs
Owner: VP Merchandising
Participants: VP Merchandising, Category Managers, Pricing (links to VS-01.2), Treasury (links to VS-18), Supply (links to VS-02), Marketing (links to VS-14)
Source: workflow W3418 — Rapid Commodity-Shock Price Response &amp; Margin Recovery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3418_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3418_Lane1" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3418_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3418_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3418_Lane2" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3418_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3418_Lane3" name="Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3418_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3418_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3418_Start5" name="Market shock (W3407); sudden cost surge; supply disruption (links to VS-69/VS-02.3)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3418_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3418_Task6" name="Treasury/Procurement alert the rapid-response group on a commodity shock (e.g…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Treasury/Procurement alert the rapid-response group on a commodity shock (e.g., +20% steel, oil spike, cement allocation); quantify exposure impact (W3404), hedge coverage (W3412), inventory position (links to VS-05), and competitor posture (links to VS-57)
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Procurement
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3418_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3418_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3418_Task7" name="VP Merchandising/Pricing decide the price response: emergency SRP adjustment…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VP Merchandising/Pricing decide the price response: emergency SRP adjustment (links to VS-01.2), temporary surcharge, promo hold, or hold price using inventory/hedge buffer; execute via VS-01.2/W40 within authority, respect DTI rules (links to VS-22/W468), and communicate to stores/ecommerce
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising / Pricing
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3418_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3418_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3418_Task8" name="Merchandising/Marketing manage customer communication (links to VS-14.3) and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Merchandising/Marketing manage customer communication (links to VS-14.3) and competitor response (links to VS-57); Treasury execute emergency hedge/buy (links to W3410/W3412) if warranted; track margin recovery and report to executives (links to VS-33.2) and the post-event review (W3416)
Responsible (R): Merchandising / Treasury / Marketing
Accountable (A): CFO / CEO
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3418_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3418_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3418_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3418_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3418_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-549 (ensure controlled execution — Input-Cost Pass-Through, Margin Protection &amp; Risk Analytics (PA-106.3).) | - operational: pre-defined triggers and authority; operational: measured, value-driven response
Owner: VP Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3418_Assoc11" sourceRef="W3418_Annotation10" targetRef="W3418_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
